hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17883","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the pots of the People of the Book, and he said: If you find no other than them, then wash and cook. And he asked him about the meat of donkeys, and he forbade him that, and every predator with fangs."
"17884","Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Dawud, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in the Hereafter are the best of you in character. And indeed the most hateful of you to me and the farthest of you from me in the Hereafter are the worst of you in character: the chatterers, the pompous, the grandiloquent."
"17885","Yazid narrated to us: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he says: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of hunting. He said: If you send your dog and mention the name of Allah, and it holds for you, then eat. He said: I said: Even if it kills? He said: Even if it kills. He said: I said: We are people of shooting. He said: What your bow returns to you, eat. He said: I said: We are people of travel; we pass by Jews and Christians and Magians and find no vessels other than theirs. He said: If you find no other than them, wash them with water, then eat and drink in them."
"17886","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from his father, he said: I heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard him say, while in Fustat during the caliphate of Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah had raided the people against Constantinople, and he said: By Allah, this nation will not be incapable of half a day, when you see Sham as the table of one man and his household, then at that is the conquest of Constantinople."
"17887","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, he said: 'Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and the meat of every predator with fangs."
"17888","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Zabr, narrated to us that he heard Muslim ibn Mishkam say: Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani narrated to us, he said: The people, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stopping-place and encamped, would disperse from him in the ravines and valleys, so he stood among us and said: Indeed your dispersing in the ravines, that is only from Satan. He said: After that, when they alighted they would draw together, until you would say: If you spread a cloak over them it would cover them, or the like of that."
"17889","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me such and such land in Sham; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not yet prevailed over it then. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not hear what this one says? Abu Tha'labah said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you shall surely prevail over it. He said: He wrote it for him. He said: I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, our land is a land of hunting, so I send my trained dog and my dog that is not trained. He said: If you send your trained dog and name, then eat what your trained dog holds for you, even if it kills. And if you send your dog that is not trained and you reach its slaughter, then eat. And eat what your arrow returns to you, even if it kills, and name Allah. He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, our land is a land of People of the Book, and they eat pork and drink wine, so what shall I do with their vessels and pots? He said: If you find no other than them, rinse them and cook in them and drink. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us of what is forbidden to us? He said: Do not eat the meat of domestic donkeys nor every predator with fangs."
"17890","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every predator with fangs."
"17891","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, from the hadith of Abu Idris ibn Abdullah in the caliphate of Abd al-Malik, that Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid every predator with fangs."
"17892","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating every predator with fangs."
"17893","Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah informed us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that he narrated to them, he said: I campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Khaybar, and the people were hungry, so we found there domestic donkeys and slaughtered them. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed, so he ordered Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, and he called among the people that the meat of domestic donkeys is not lawful for whoever bears witness that I am the Messenger of Allah. He said: And we found in their sides onions and garlic, and the people were hungry and exerted, so they went in the evening, and the scent of the mosque was onions and garlic. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this foul plant, let him not approach us. And he said: Plunder is not lawful, nor is lawful every predator with fangs, nor is lawful the animal tied as a target."
"17894","Zayd ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: I heard Muslim ibn Mishkam, he said: I heard al-Khushani say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what is lawful for me and forbidden to me. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked up and down at me, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Righteousness is what the soul settles to and the heart is tranquil with, and sin is what the soul does not settle to and the heart is not tranquil with, even if the muftis give you fatwa. And he said: Do not approach the meat of the domestic donkey nor a predator with fangs."
"17895","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Dawud informed us, from Makhul, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me are the best of you in character. And indeed the most hateful of you to me and the farthest of you from me are the worst of you in character: the chatterers, the grandiloquent, the pompous."
"17896","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us: Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you shoot your arrow and it is absent for three nights, then you find it, eat unless it has stunk."
"17897","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-'Ala' ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Mishkam narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what is lawful for me of what is forbidden to me. He said: He looked up and down at me, then said: Nuwaybitah. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Nuwaybitah of good or Nuwaybitah of evil? He said: Rather Nuwaybitah of good. Do not eat the meat of the domestic donkey nor every predator with fangs."
"17898","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Busr ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated to me, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, the like of that."
"17899","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, and Ibn Shihab narrated to me that Abu Idris informed him that Abu Tha'labah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."
"17900","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Al-Zubaydi narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Sayf al-Kala'i, from Abu Idris 'A'idhullah ibn Abdullah al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he looked up and down at me, then said: Nuwaybitah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Nuwaybitah of good or Nuwaybitah of evil? He said: Rather Nuwaybitah of good. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of hunting, so I send my trained dog; of it what I reach its slaughter and of it what I do not reach its slaughter, and I shoot my arrow; of it what I reach its slaughter and of it what I do not reach its slaughter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat what your hand and your bow and your trained dog return to you, slaughtered or not slaughtered."
"17901","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, he said, al-Numan ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring on my hand and began tapping his hand with a stick he had. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then turned his attention away from him, so he took the ring and threw it away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked and did not see it on his finger, and said, I think we have only hurt you and caused you loss."
"17902","Muhanna ibn Abd al-Hamid and Affan narrated to us, and this is the wording of Muhanna, he said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, that he said, O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, shall we cook in their pots and drink in their vessels. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, If you find nothing else, then wash them with water and cook in them. He said, O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game, so what shall we do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, When you release your trained dog and mention the name of Allah Almighty and it kills, then eat. And if it is untrained, then slaughter and eat. And when you shoot your arrow and mention the name of Allah and it kills, then eat."
"17903","Wahb narrated to me, he said, my father narrated to us, he said, I heard al-Numan narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, he said, A man sat beside the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a gold ring on his hand, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tapped his hand with a rod in his hand. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him, so the man threw away his ring. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him and said, Where is your ring. He said, I threw it away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I think we have hurt you and caused you loss."
"17904","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, that he said, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, shall we eat in their vessels. And we are in a land of game; I hunt with my bow, and I hunt with my trained dog, and I hunt with my untrained dog, so tell me what is lawful. He said, As for what you mentioned, that you are in the land of the People of the Book and eat in their vessels, if you find vessels other than theirs then do not eat in theirs, and if you find nothing but their vessels then wash them and eat in them. And as for what you mentioned, that you are in a land of game, if you hunt with your bow and mention the name of Allah then eat. And what you hunt with your trained dog, mention the name of Allah then eat. And what you hunt with your untrained dog, if you reach it in time to slaughter it then eat."
